---An `LocList` provides access to all active LocEntities in the game world, as well as several methods to search for
---entities.
---
---See each method for examples on how to use this list.
---
---Important: Not all locations in the game are available as an entity. Only locations which are considered `active` are
---accessible, such locations that animate, are interactable, or can be modified by the server or variable state. The
---remaining location are combined into larger static locations, to be rendered more optimally.
---
---Info: All methods return an array of LocEntities.
---
---Warning: These functions can return a large number of results and may impact performance if called frequently. Prefer
---using methods where distance testing is available, such as LocList.ByDistance or LocList.Filter with `coordGrid` and
---`range` tests provided.
---@class LocList
LocList = {}

---Returns all active LocEntities in the game world in an array.
---@return LocEntity[] # An array of LocEntities.
function LocList.All() end

---Returns any LocEntity with a display name matching the given `name` value.
---
---String matches are case-insensitive. Matches are exact unless wildcard characters `?` and/or `*` are provided.
---@param name string The string to match against `LocEntity.displayName`.
---@return LocEntity[] # An array of LocEntities.
function LocList.ByName(name) end

---Returns any LocEntity within `range` tiles of the given `coordGrid` value.
---
---Exact coord matches should use a value of `0` for `range`.
---@param coordGrid CoordGrid The coordinate at which to centre the distance search.
---@param range integer The maximum tile distance from the given coord which an LocEntity must be. A value of `0` tests only the exact coordinate provided.
---@param sameLevel boolean Whether to only consider LocEntities on the same level as the given coordinate or LocEntities on all levels.
---@return LocEntity[] # An array of LocEntities.
function LocList.ByDistance(coordGrid, range, sameLevel) end

---Returns any LocEntity that uses the given LocType config.
---
---Info: If the LocEntity has a valid `LocEntity.config` then this will test against `LocEntity.config`. If not, then
---the value for `LocEntity.parentConfig` will be tested against instead.
---@param locType LocType The config to look for when testing LocEntities.
---@return LocEntity[] # An array of LocEntities.
function LocList.ByConfig(locType) end

---Info: If the LocEntity has a valid `LocEntity.config` then this will test against `LocEntity.configID`. If not, then
---the value for `LocEntity.parentConfigID` will be tested against instead.
---
---Info: Only `LocEntity.configID` is tested, while `LocEntity.parentConfigID` is not tested against.
---@param locTypeID integer The config ID to look for when testing LocEntities.
---@return LocEntity[] # An array of LocEntities.
function LocList.ByConfigID(locTypeID) end

---Returns any LocEntity that uses the given LocType config.
---
---Info: Only `LocEntity.parentConfig` is tested, while `LocEntity.config` is not tested against.
---@param locType LocType The config to look for when testing LocEntities.
---@return LocEntity[] # An array of LocEntities.
function LocList.ByParentConfig(locType) end

---Returns any LocEntity that uses the given LocType config ID.
---
---Info: Only `LocEntity.parentConfigID` is tested, while `LocEntity.configID` is not tested against.
---@param locTypeID integer The config ID to look for when testing LocEntities.
---@return LocEntity[] # An array of LocEntities.
function LocList.ByParentConfigID(locTypeID) end

---Returns any LocEntity that matches all tests in the `filterSet` table.
---
---Available tests are:
---
---Tests can be combined as shown below:
---
---Info: Tests are inclusive. All must pass in order for the LocEntity to be included in the return array.
---@param filterSet LocListFilterSettings A table of key-value pairs which describe individual tests to perform.
---@return LocEntity[] # An array of LocEntities.
function LocList.Filter(filterSet) end

---The keys `LocList.Filter` takes in its table.
---@class LocListFilterSettings
---@field name string? A name to match against `LocEntity.displayName`. `{ name = "*lumbridge*" }` See LocList.ByName()
---@field coordGrid CoordGrid? A coordinate to test entity distance from. If `range` is not provided, the default value of `range` will be `0`. If `sameLevel` is not provided, the default value of `sameLevel` will be `false`. `{ coordGrid = CoordGrid._0_50_50_32_32 }` See LocList.ByDistance()
---@field range integer? Ignored if `coordGrid` key is not provided. `{ range = 4 }` See LocList.ByDistance()
---@field sameLevel boolean? Ignored if `coordGrid` key is not provided. `{ sameLevel = true }` See LocList.ByDistance()
---@field config LocType? The config to match against `LocEntity.config`. `{ config = config.Loc.FFH_WILLOW_TREE_TRUNK }` See LocList.ByConfig()
---@field configID integer? The config ID to match against `LocEntity.configID`. `{ configID = id.Loc.FFH_WILLOW_TREE_TRUNK }` See LocList.ByConfigID()
---@field parentConfig LocType? The config to match against `LocEntity.parentConfig`. `{ parentConfig = config.Loc.GARDEN_LUMBRIDGE_STATUE }` See LocList.ByParentConfig()
---@field parentConfigID integer? The config ID to match against `LocEntity.parentConfigID`. `{ parentConfigID = id.Loc.GARDEN_LUMBRIDGE_STATUE }` See LocList.ByParentConfigID()
---@field func (fun(locEntity: LocEntity): boolean)|nil A function which returns a boolean, and which takes a LocEntity as its only parameter. This function is called for every entity, and any call that returns `true` will include that LocEntity in the return array. `function willowFinder(locEntity) { return locEntity.config == config.Loc.FFH_WILLOW_TREE_TRUNK }` `{ func = willowFinder }`
